  "claim_boundary": "The five-level two-term modal study is an offline empirical diagnostic for smooth linear circuits with homogeneous dynamic units and a qualified symmetric modal basis. Qualified Loop 5G groups retain their existing one-term estimate. Rejected groups fit Y_f = Y_inf + C f^-2 + D f^-q using native factors 2, 4, 8, and 16, while native factor 32 remains excluded from fitting and is used only as a holdout gate and residual envelope. Secondary orders 3 and 4 are common policies across every family and size. The report publishes design conditioning, training residual, holdout residual, contribution magnitudes, and fallback source. Error estimates conservatively add the absolute primary contribution, absolute secondary contribution, and a residual envelope amplified by the deterministic intercept leverage. Ill-conditioned, under-resolved, non-finite, or holdout-inconsistent fits remain uncovered. The study does not alter a BAB-CS runtime profile and does not establish a formal exact-trajectory enclosure."
